# Agent working files
implementation_plan.md

# Machine-specific agent configuration. `.codex/config.toml` holds an absolute
# path to a Godot binary on one developer's desktop, so it is wrong in every
# other clone by construction.
#
# **`.agents/` IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE.** The working rules two agents share --
# the checkpoint procedure above all -- must be reviewable by both, or the next
# divergence is invisible the way the last one was: two copies of `/save`, one
# telling its agent to checkpoint into `CLAUDE.md` and the other into `AGENTS.md`.
# Configuration is personal; process is not.
.codex/

# Tuning codegen intermediates — derived from TUNABLES.md, regenerated every run.
/tools/tuning_codegen/*.json

# `> /dev/null` on Windows. Git Bash resolves it; cmd and PowerShell do not, so a
# redirect from either writes a literal "dev/null" file at the repo root — or a
# "dev/null/" directory, when something copies into it. A worktree here collected
# four git hooks that way, and they were untracked and unignored, one `git add -A`
# from being committed.
#
# Narrow on purpose: "/dev/" would silently swallow a real dev/ folder if anyone
# ever adds one, and this project has enough silent things in it already.
/dev/null
/dev/null/
